# A teaching example. GitHub reads the first CODEOWNERS it finds in .github/,
# the repository root or docs/, and asks its owners to review a pull request
# that touches a matching file. Patterns follow gitignore rules and the LAST
# matching line wins, so put the general line first.
#
# Replace @your-github-handle with your login, and add a collaborator's handle
# next to the folder you want them to look at.
#
# In a private camp this only works on GitHub Pro or above; in a public one it
# works on every plan. Making it do something also needs a branch protection
# rule with "Require review from Code Owners" (Settings, Branches).

*                     @your-github-handle

# The notes are yours; the game is the thing other people will open.
/workspace/game/      @your-github-handle
/vault/               @your-github-handle
